return {h=88,w=2100,cr=45,hc=25,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"mineral"},st={35,45,160,30,45,70},ab={{69,0},{5,0},{133,1}},genus={en="Rock Snake Pokémon",es="Pokémon Serpiente Roca",pt="Pokémon Serpente de Pedra"},flavor={en={[1]="As it grows, the stone portions of its body harden to become similar to a diamond, but colored black.",[2]="As it grows, the stone portions of its body harden to become similar to a diamond, but colored black.",[3]="Burrows at high speed in search of food. The tunnels it leaves are used as homes by DIGLETTs.",[4]="It twists and squirms through the ground. The thunderous roar of its tunneling echoes a long way.",[5]="It rapidly bores through the ground at 50 mph by squirming and twisting its massive, rugged body.",[6]="As it digs through the ground, it absorbs many hard objects. This is what makes its body so solid.",[7]="ONIX has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling. As it grows older, its body becomes increasingly rounder and smoother.",[8]="ONIX has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling. As it grows older, its body becomes increasingly rounder and smoother.",[9]="There is a magnet in its brain that prevents an ONIX from losing direction while tunneling. As it grows older, its body becomes steadily rounder and smoother.",[10]="It usually lives underground. It searches for food while boring its way through the ground at 50 miles per hour.",[11]="As it grows, the stone portions of its body harden to become similar to black-colored diamonds.",[12]="When it travels underground, it causes rumbling and tremors. It can move at 50 mph.",[13]="It squirms through the ground using its long and rugged body. It always eats while burrowing.",[14]="It burrows through the ground at a speed of 50 mph while feeding on large boulders.",[15]="It twists and squirms through the ground. The thunderous roar of its tunneling echoes a long way.",[16]="It rapidly bores through the ground at 50 mph by squirming and twisting its massive, rugged body.",[17]="It burrows through the ground at a speed of 50 mph while feeding on large boulders.",[18]="It burrows through the ground at a speed of 50 mph while feeding on large boulders.",[21]="Opening its large mouth, it ingests massive amounts of soil and creates long tunnels.",[22]="Opening its large mouth, it ingests massive amounts of soil and creates long tunnels.",[23]="Burrows at high speed in search of food. The tunnels it leaves are used as homes by Diglett.",[24]="It usually lives underground. It searches for food while boring its way through the ground at 50 miles per hour.",[25]="Onix has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling. As it grows older, its body becomes increasingly rounder and smoother.",[26]="Onix has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling. As it grows older, its body becomes increasingly rounder and smoother.",[31]="Burrows at high speed in search of food. The tunnels it leaves are used as homes by Diglett.",[32]="Burrows at high speed in search of food. The tunnels it leaves are used as homes by Diglett.",[33]="As it digs through the ground, it absorbs many hard objects. This is what makes its body so solid.",[34]="It rapidly bores through the ground at 50 mph by squirming and twisting its massive, rugged body.",[39]="This chain of immense stones resembles a giant serpent. Tremors shake the earth above as it burrows deep beneath the ground, feeding on boulders as it goes."},es={[23]="Cava a gran velocidad en busca de comida. Los túneles que deja son usados por los Diglett.",[24]="Suele vivir bajo tierra. Va buscando comida a medida que se va abriendo camino a 80 km por hora.",[25]="Onix tiene un imán en el cerebro, que actúa como una brújula para no perder la orientación cuando está